  "note": {
    "text": "Every baby goes at their own pace, so these may come sooner or later for yours.",
    "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-1mo.html"
  },
  "periods": [
    {
      "age": 1,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Your baby spends most of the time eating, sleeping, crying and filling diapers.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Developmental-Milestones-1-Month.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Reflexes are strong. Startling, rooting and gripping your finger are all built in.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-newborn.html",
          "additional_source_urls": [
            "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/002004.htm"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby can see about a foot away, just far enough to find your face.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 2,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Crying is how your baby asks to be held, fed, changed or put down to sleep.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-newborn.html"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your voice and touch can soothe your baby.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-newborn.html"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may turn toward your voice or other familiar sounds.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-newborn.html",
          "additional_source_urls": [
            "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 3,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Movements are often jerky or jittery. Your baby can't control most of them yet.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby doesn't have much neck control yet and needs your help to support their head.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hands stay mostly in tight fists.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Developmental-Milestones-1-Month.aspx",
          "additional_source_urls": [
            "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-1mo.html"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 4,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "By the end of the first month, your baby is much more alert and responsive.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Developmental-Milestones-1-Month.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may prefer faces to other patterns, and likes high contrast.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Developmental-Milestones-1-Month.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Eyes may wander or occasionally cross at this age.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Developmental-Milestones-1-Month.aspx",
          "review_note": "AAP's wording for about 1 month. Do you want a line on when to mention this to the pediatrician?"
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 5,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Your baby may recognize your voice.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-1mo.html"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pleasant sounds, like music, can make your baby more alert.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-1mo.html"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hands may come within range of your baby's eyes and mouth.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Developmental-Milestones-1-Month.aspx"
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 6,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "A first real smile can come from around now.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx",
          "review_note": "AAP says 'around her sixth week.' Could worry a parent if it's later. AAP's emotional development page says 'by the second month.'"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may wave their arms around when excited.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby spends a lot of the day watching and listening to the people around them.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Emotional-and-Social-Development-Birth-to-3-Months.aspx"
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 7,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Early grins and grimaces are turning into real signals of pleasure.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Emotional-and-Social-Development-Birth-to-3-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hands are catching your baby's attention. After many tries, they may reach the mouth.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may seem to smile past you. Looking away is a way of taking it all in.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Emotional-and-Social-Development-Birth-to-3-Months.aspx"
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 8,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Most babies this age can lift their head when on their tummy.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx",
          "additional_source_urls": [
            "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-2mos.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You may hear sounds other than crying.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-2mos.html"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may seem happy to see you.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-2mos.html"
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 9,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Movement is getting smoother and wigglier as some newborn reflexes fade.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may watch you as you move around.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-2mos.html"
        },
        {
          "text": "Babies often look round and chubby at this age.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Physical-Appearance-and-Growth-1-To-3-Months.aspx"
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 10,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Your baby may hold your gaze for longer now.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Emotional-and-Social-Development-Birth-to-3-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hands open more often.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-2mos.html",
          "additional_source_urls": [
            "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may look at a toy for several seconds.",
          "source_url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/development-2mos.html"
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 11,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Smiling gives your baby a way besides crying to tell you things.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Emotional-and-Social-Development-Birth-to-3-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may prefer certain people and give others a more curious look.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Emotional-and-Social-Development-Birth-to-3-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may enjoy kicking their legs more actively.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "age": 12,
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Your baby's whole body may look more relaxed, with legs straightening out from the newborn curl.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your baby may swipe at objects hanging just out of reach.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx"
        },
        {
          "text": "The startle reflex has probably faded by now.",
          "source_url": "https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/baby/Pages/Movement-Birth-to-Three-Months.aspx",
          "additional_source_urls": [
            "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/002004.htm"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "review_status": "DRAFT"
    }
  ]
}